--TEST--
A namespace segment, an interface, a type alias and a class in the wrong case are each refused, so are a constant that is not SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE and a property, a parameter, a method and a local that are not camelCase, a name beginning with `_` is refused under its own category's rule, `__construct` is refused by name, and every one of the twelve is reported rather than the first stopping the file (`rule:core-api/identifier-casing`, `rule:core-api/casing-has-no-suppression`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:programs/names-and-casing
// `rule:core-api/identifier-casing`: a namespace segment, an interface, a
// type alias and a class are each PascalCase, and a mismatch is a hard error
// carrying the rename the compiler derived for it.
namespace app\Billing;

interface priced {}

type order_id = int;

class order_line {
    // A class constant is SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE; a property, a parameter, a
    // method and a local are camelCase.
    public const int maxQuantity = 1;
    public int $UnitPrice = 0;

    // The constructor is spelled `constructor`, and PHP's `__construct` is
    // refused by name rather than as a casing mismatch.
    public function __construct(int $UnitPrice) {
        $this->UnitPrice = $UnitPrice;
    }

    public function TotalPrice(int $Quantity): int {
        return $this->UnitPrice * $Quantity;
    }

    // No identifier may begin with `_`, which needs no rule of its own: a
    // leading underscore is not camelCase, and the rename drops it.
    public function _hidden(): int {
        return 1;
    }
}

// `rule:core-api/casing-has-no-suppression`: nothing in the file above turns
// any of these off, and every one of the twelve is reported.
int $_scratch = 1;
echo $_scratch, "\n";
--EXPECT--

